Source binding: const designSchema; version borsal.design/0.1. This is a typed contract, not an answer template.
Output one JSON object matching Root. Every listed field is REQUIRED unless marked ?. All objects reject extra fields. Arrays may be empty unless min/len says otherwise.
ID matches ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$; TEXT is a nonempty trimmed string; N is finite number; I is safe integer; P=[N,N]. Coordinates/dimensions are cm; x right/y up; negative coordinates allowed. Types/aliases below are notation, not literal output values.
Source=({kind:"SCRAP",scrapId:ID} OR {kind:"STOCK",availability:"NOT_CHECKED"})
Material=({type:"WOVEN_FABRIC",specs:{fiber:"COTTON"|"POLYESTER"|"BLEND",weave:"PLAIN"|"TWILL"|"SATIN",weightGsm:N>0}} OR {type:"LINING_FABRIC",specs:{fiber:"COTTON"|"POLYESTER"|"BLEND",weightGsm:N>0}} OR {type:"WEBBING",specs:{fiber:"COTTON"|"POLYESTER"|"BLEND",widthCm:N>0}} OR {type:"ZIPPER",specs:{lengthCm:N>0,toothType:"COIL"|"METAL",endType:"CLOSED"|"OPEN"}} OR {type:"THREAD",specs:{fiber:"COTTON"|"POLYESTER"|"BLEND",tex:N>0}} OR {type:"BUTTON",specs:{diameterCm:N>0,material:"METAL"|"RESIN"|"WOOD"}} OR {type:"HARDWARE",specs:{kind:"D_RING"|"SWIVEL_HOOK"|"MAGNETIC_SNAP"|"TURN_LOCK"|"RIVET"|"BAG_FOOT",finish:"BRASS"|"NICKEL"|"BLACK",sizeCm:N>0}} OR {type:"INTERFACING",specs:{weightGsm:N>0,bond:"FUSIBLE"|"SEW_IN"}})
BOM={id:ID,source:Source,material:Material,quantity:{value:N>0,unit:"cm"|"cm2"|"piece"}}
EdgeRef={pieceId:ID,copy:I>0,edgeIds:ID[] min=1,direction:"FORWARD"|"REVERSE"}
Anchor={pieceId:ID,copy:I>0,point:P}
Fold={id:ID,type:"HEM"|"BOX"|"PLEAT",from:P,to:P,allowanceCm:N>0}
Piece={id:ID,bomId:ID,cutCount:I>0,outlineBasis:"SEAM_LINE",outline:{start:P,segments:({id:ID,type:"LINE",to:P} OR {id:ID,type:"CUBIC_BEZIER",control1:P,control2:P,to:P})[] min=2},seamAllowanceCm:N>=0,grainDirectionDeg:N>=0<180,folds:Fold[]}
Component={id:ID,role:"BODY"|"GUSSET"|"BASE"|"POCKET"|"FLAP"|"STRAP"|"HANDLE"|"LINING"|"DIVIDER"|"REINFORCEMENT",pieceIds:ID[] min=1}
Assembly=({id:ID,type:"SEAM",sides:[EdgeRef,EdgeRef],threadBomId:ID} OR {id:ID,type:"ATTACH",from:Anchor,to:Anchor,threadBomId:ID} OR {id:ID,type:"INSTALL",bomId:ID,anchors:Anchor[] min=1})
Feature={id:ID,kind:"BODY"|"GUSSET"|"FOLD"|"POCKET"|"FLAP"|"CLOSURE"|"STRAP"|"HANDLE"|"COMPARTMENT"|"STRUCTURE"|"SURFACE",intent:TEXT,componentIds:ID[],bomIds:ID[]}
Limitation={id:ID,featureId:ID,status:"PARTIAL"|"UNSUPPORTED",reason:TEXT,missingInformation:TEXT[] min=1}
Creative={description:TEXT,aesthetic:TEXT[] min=1,intendedUse:TEXT}
Technical={dimensionUnit:"cm",evidence:"ILLUSTRATIVE_ONLY",overallDimensions:{width:N>0,height:N>0,depth:N>0},scrapSources:{id:ID}[] len=1,bom:BOM[] min=1,components:Component[] min=1,patternPieces:Piece[] min=1,assembly:Assembly[],features:Feature[] min=1}
Root={schemaVersion:"borsal.design/0.1",id:ID,name:TEXT,category:"SHOULDER_BAG"|"TOTE_BAG",creative:Creative,technical:Technical,limitations:Limitation[]}
Cross-field rules: IDs unique within scrapSources, bom, components, patternPieces, assembly, features and root limitations; edge/fold IDs unique within a piece. Each piece belongs to exactly one component. Every component, piece, BOM, feature and scrap reference must exist.
ONE declared physical scrap; at least one woven-fabric SCRAP BOM entry, all tied to that scrapId; at least one pattern piece uses it. Multiple cut pieces/copies may come from it. STOCK availability stays NOT_CHECKED.
BOM quantity units: WOVEN_FABRIC/LINING_FABRIC/INTERFACING -> cm2; WEBBING/THREAD -> cm; ZIPPER/BUTTON/HARDWARE -> integer piece. Quantity/spec dimensions >0; seamAllowanceCm>=0; fold.allowanceCm>0.
Pattern pieces require WOVEN_FABRIC, LINING_FABRIC or INTERFACING. Ready-made webbing/buttons/hardware are BOM entries used by INSTALL and Feature, NOT fabric patterns or invented components. Fabric-cut straps/handles may have real pattern pieces.
CLOSURE is a Feature kind, NOT a Component role. Do not invent a component for a button; reference its BOM entry and body anchors.
Each outline needs >=2 ordered LINE/CUBIC_BEZIER segments and must explicitly close: final segment.to equals outline.start. The seamAllowanceCm scalar is not a generated cutting offset.
EdgeRef requires pieceId, copy, edgeIds, direction, not id. copy is 1..cutCount. Every edgeId must match a segment.id in that piece. Anchor requires pieceId, copy, point. SEAM/ATTACH require threadBomId pointing to a THREAD BOM entry, never outer fabric.
limitations is REQUIRED at the JSON ROOT, never technical.limitations. Each limitation.featureId references an existing Feature; reason and EVERY missingInformation entry must be informative nonempty text, with at least one entry. Use [] only when no feature is partial/unsupported.
Preserve EVERY brief requirement technically where supported: geometry for silhouette/opening; body-connected anchors for straps/closures; BOM specifications for material intent. Creative prose alone is insufficient. For unmodeled intent, keep a named Feature and honest PARTIAL/UNSUPPORTED limitation; do not invent unrequested requirements as limitations.
Dimensions/quantities are illustrative; never claim manufacturing feasibility. No predefined bag templates or completed examples are supplied.

